WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.299
Angela Merkel's announcement in October came
as a surprise.

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:09.480
Europe's longest-serving elected leader may
achieve what no modern day chancellor has

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.900
managed before: a controlled exit from politics.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:24.210
I won't run again as party leader at the next
CDU party conference in Hamburg.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:30.279
This fourth term is my last as chancellor
of Germany."

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:34.940
Merkel became the first woman at the top of
the CDU in the year 2000.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.480
Surprising nearly everyone the newcomer from
the East led her party's break with its political

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:46.930
idol Helmut Kohl over a party funding scandal
-- even though Kohl was her mentor.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:52.220
The determination and power instinct the party
SAW there -- was also what it would GET over

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.970
the 18 years.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.630
Those who refused to accept that the CDU was
no longer a Gentlemens' club, soon learned

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:04.150
the hard way: one by one, her competitors
had to go.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:10.370
After becoming Chancellor in 2005, Merkel
took her CDU party on a political journey,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:16.410
many criticized as a shift to the left -- shedding
conservative benchmark policies like military

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:23.700
conscription and performing a U-turn on nuclear
energy over the Fukushima desaster in Japan.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:30.140
By then her role as party leader and her perception
as chancellor had long became inseperable.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:36.060
Merkel's political brand as the one who guarantees
stability was born.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.190
In the midst of the Greek debt crisis she
defended risking Bbillions of German tax payers

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:45.890
money by claiming there was no alternative.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.580
There is no alternative to supporting Greece
to secure the financial stability of the Euro.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.210
Die zu beschließenden Griechenlandhilfen
sind alternativlos, um die Finanzstabilität

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.390
der Eurozone zu sichern.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:59.060
Her "no alternative" reasoning also saw her
keeping Germany's borders open during what

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:05.440
became known as the migration crisis in 2015
-- THE political challenge that still defines

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.959
her leadership of her party and Germany as
a whole.

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:15.090
If we were to now doubt that can do this -- considering
our European responsibility, our humanitarian

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.850
responsibility and our responsibility for
Germany -- then we wouldn't be the Christian

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.700
Democratic Union of Germany.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:27.000
But we are, and that's why we can can do this.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.959
Merkel herself was long seen as conservative
party leader "without an alternative" that

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:33.450
could replace her.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:39.200
The fact there are now several credible candidates
is also fuelling speculation over how much

00:02:39.200 --> 00:04:44.589
longer she can

00:04:44.589 --> 00:06:40.310
remain chancellor.

